{"schema":"learning-v2-theory.v1","lesson":3,"lang":"id","title":"Benda: a, an, the, this, these","sections":[{"num":"01","title":"Apa yang akan kamu pelajari","defaultOpen":true,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Di pelajaran ini kamu belajar menyebut benda di sekitarmu: «ini kursi», «ini tiket», «charger ini», «bunga-bunga itu segar», «kesalahannya di sini», «ini cangkir merah». Bahasa Inggris memakai kata-kata kecil di depan benda: a, an, the, this, that."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"It is a chair.","translation":"Ini kursi.","hi":"a"},{"en":"They are tickets.","translation":"Ini tiket.","hi":"tickets"},{"en":"This is a charger.","translation":"Ini charger. *(di tanganku)*","hi":"This"},{"en":"Those flowers are fresh.","translation":"Bunga-bunga itu segar.","hi":"Those"},{"en":"It is a red cup.","translation":"Ini cangkir merah.","hi":"red"}]}]},{"num":"02","title":"Satu benda — di depannya a","defaultOpen":true,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Kita cukup bilang «Ini kursi». Dalam bahasa Inggris, di depan satu benda hampir selalu ada a kecil: It is a chair. a tidak diterjemahkan — artinya kira-kira «sebuah». Tanpa a kalimatnya terasa bolong."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"It is","accent":true},{"text":"a","accent":true},{"text":"benda","accent":true}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"It is a chair.","translation":"Ini kursi.","hi":"a"},{"en":"It's a lamp.","translation":"Ini lampu.","hi":"a"},{"en":"Is it a table?","translation":"Ini meja?","hi":"a"},{"en":"It is a key.","translation":"Ini kunci.","hi":"a"},{"en":"It is not a window.","translation":"Ini bukan jendela.","hi":"a"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"It is chair.","right":"It is a chair."},{"wrong":"Is it table?","right":"Is it a table?"}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"Dalam pertanyaan dan kalimat «bukan», a tetap di tempatnya: Is it a table? It is not a window."}]},{"num":"03","title":"a atau an — ditentukan bunyi pertama","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Kalau kata dimulai dengan bunyi vokal, ganti a dengan an: an armchair, an oven, an umbrella. Dengan begitu lebih mudah diucapkan, tidak tersandung di antara dua vokal."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"It is an armchair.","translation":"Ini kursi berlengan.","hi":"an"},{"en":"Is it an oven?","translation":"Ini oven?","hi":"an"},{"en":"It's an umbrella.","translation":"Ini payung.","hi":"an"},{"en":"It is an earring.","translation":"Ini anting.","hi":"an"},{"en":"It's an egg.","translation":"Ini telur.","hi":"an"},{"en":"It is an invoice.","translation":"Ini faktur.","hi":"an"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"It is a oven.","right":"It is an oven."},{"wrong":"It's a egg.","right":"It's an egg."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"It's","after":"umbrella.","options":["a","an","the"],"answer":"an","why":"umbrella dimulai dengan bunyi vokal, jadi an."}}]},{"num":"04","title":"Bunyi, bukan huruf","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Perhatikan bunyinya, bukan hurufnya. Di hour, huruf h tidak dibaca — bunyinya «auer», jadi an hour. Sedangkan uniform dan euro dimulai dengan bunyi «y» («yuniform», «yuro») — itu bukan vokal, jadi a."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"It is an hour.","translation":"Satu jam.","hi":"an"},{"en":"Is it a uniform?","translation":"Itu seragam?","hi":"a"},{"en":"It's a euro.","translation":"Ini satu euro.","hi":"a"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"It is a hour.","right":"It is an hour."},{"wrong":"It's an euro.","right":"It's a euro."}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"Cara mudah: ucapkan kata itu keras-keras. Dimulai dengan «a, e, o, u» — an. Dimulai dengan «y» atau konsonan — a."}]},{"num":"05","title":"Banyak benda: tambah s, buang a","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Kita bilang «beberapa tiket» atau «tiket-tiket», kata «tiket» sendiri tidak berubah. Bahasa Inggris mengubahnya: tambah s — ticket → tickets. Dan a dibuang, karena a artinya «satu». Penjepitnya juga berubah: satu benda — it is, banyak — they are."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"They are","accent":true},{"text":"benda + s","accent":false}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"They are tickets.","translation":"Ini tiket.","hi":"tickets"},{"en":"Are they coins?","translation":"Ini koin?","hi":"coins"},{"en":"The cards are new.","translation":"Kartunya baru.","hi":"cards"},{"en":"They are towels.","translation":"Ini handuk.","hi":"towels"},{"en":"They are spoons.","translation":"Ini sendok.","hi":"spoons"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"They are ticket.","right":"They are tickets."},{"wrong":"They are a tickets.","right":"They are tickets."},{"wrong":"It is tickets.","right":"They are tickets."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"word_bank","kind":"word_bank","prompt":"Kurir memberimu beberapa tiket. Katakan: «Ini tiket».","answer":["They","are","tickets"],"slotLabels":["siapa","penjepit","apa"],"distractors":["a","ticket"]}}]},{"num":"06","title":"Kapan perlu es","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Kalau kata berakhir dengan s, sh, atau ch, s saja tidak bisa diucapkan. Maka ditambah es, dan muncul satu suku kata lagi: bus → buses, dish → dishes, watch → watches. Terdengar: «basis», «disyis»."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"They are buses.","translation":"Ini bus.","hi":"buses"},{"en":"Are they dishes?","translation":"Ini piring?","hi":"dishes"},{"en":"The watches are old.","translation":"Jam tangannya sudah tua.","hi":"watches"},{"en":"They are glasses.","translation":"Ini gelas.","hi":"glasses"},{"en":"Are they brushes?","translation":"Ini sikat?","hi":"brushes"},{"en":"The benches are here.","translation":"Bangkunya di sini.","hi":"benches"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"They are buss.","right":"They are buses."},{"wrong":"The watchs are old.","right":"The watches are old."}]}]},{"num":"07","title":"Kapan y berubah jadi ies","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Kalau kata berakhir dengan y dan sebelumnya konsonan, y diganti ies: battery → batteries, city → cities. Bunyinya hampir sama, hanya di akhir terdengar «z»."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"They are batteries.","translation":"Ini baterai.","hi":"batteries"},{"en":"Are they countries?","translation":"Ini nama-nama negara?","hi":"countries"},{"en":"Where are the stories?","translation":"Di mana cerita-ceritanya?","hi":"stories"},{"en":"They are cities.","translation":"Ini kota-kota.","hi":"cities"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"They are batterys.","right":"They are batteries."},{"wrong":"Where are the storys?","right":"Where are the stories?"}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"Are they","after":"?","options":["countrys","countries","countryes"],"answer":"countries","why":"Sebelum y ada konsonan r, jadi y berubah jadi ies."}}]},{"num":"08","title":"this dan that: dekat atau jauh","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Dekat, bisa dijangkau tangan — this («ini»). Jauh, ditunjuk dengan jari — that («itu»). Bedanya dengan bahasa Indonesia: this dan that ada di DEPAN benda — this charger, bukan charger this."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"This is a charger.","translation":"Ini charger. *(di tangan)*","hi":"This"},{"en":"This is an adapter.","translation":"Ini adaptor.","hi":"This"},{"en":"That is a screen.","translation":"Itu layar. *(di sana)*","hi":"That"},{"en":"Is this a remote?","translation":"Ini remot?","hi":"this"},{"en":"Is that a button?","translation":"Itu tombol?","hi":"that"},{"en":"That is not a keyring.","translation":"Itu bukan gantungan kunci.","hi":"That"}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"binary","kind":"binary","question":"Layarnya tergantung di dinding ujung ruangan. Kamu bilang apa?","optionA":"This is a screen.","optionB":"That is a screen.","correct":"B","explain":"Layarnya jauh, jadi that."}}]},{"num":"09","title":"these dan those: kalau bendanya banyak","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Untuk banyak benda, this berubah jadi these, dan that jadi those. Penjepitnya are. Dekat — these are, jauh — those are."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"satu, dekat: this is","accent":false},{"text":"banyak, dekat: these are","accent":false},{"text":"satu, jauh: that is","accent":false},{"text":"banyak, jauh: those are","accent":false}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"These are shoes.","translation":"Ini sepatu. *(di depanku)*","hi":"These"},{"en":"Those are blankets.","translation":"Itu selimut. *(di sana)*","hi":"Those"},{"en":"Are these socks new?","translation":"Kaus kaki ini baru?","hi":"these"},{"en":"Those sheets are big.","translation":"Seprai-seprai itu besar.","hi":"Those"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"This are shoes.","right":"These are shoes."},{"wrong":"These is shoes.","right":"These are shoes."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"","after":"are shoes.","options":["This","These","Those"],"answer":"These","why":"Sepatunya banyak dan dekat: these."}}]},{"num":"10","title":"«Album ini», «bunga itu» — dibalik","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Kita bilang «album ini», «bunga itu» — kata penunjuknya di belakang. Bahasa Inggris menaruhnya di depan: this album, those flowers. Kalau begitu, a tidak perlu. Satu benda — this atau that; banyak — these atau those, dan katanya pakai s."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"This album is big.","translation":"Album ini besar.","hi":"This"},{"en":"These frames are cheap.","translation":"Bingkai-bingkai ini murah.","hi":"These"},{"en":"Those flowers are fresh.","translation":"Bunga-bunga itu segar.","hi":"Those"},{"en":"This building is new.","translation":"Gedung ini baru.","hi":"This"},{"en":"Is this lemon ripe?","translation":"Lemon ini sudah matang?","hi":"this"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Album this is big.","right":"This album is big."},{"wrong":"These frame are cheap.","right":"These frames are cheap."}]}]},{"num":"11","title":"a atau the","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Bahasa Indonesia tidak punya the, jadi di sinilah paling sering bingung. a — saat menyebut sesuatu pertama kali, pendengar belum tahu yang mana: A cashier is here. the — saat kalian berdua tahu yang dibicarakan: The mistake is here. Mirip akhiran «-nya» dalam «kesalahannya»."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"A cashier is here.","translation":"Ada kasir di sini.","hi":"A"},{"en":"This is a receipt.","translation":"Ini struk.","hi":"a"},{"en":"The mistake is here.","translation":"Kesalahannya di sini.","hi":"The"},{"en":"The handle is broken.","translation":"Gagangnya rusak. *(pintu ini)*","hi":"The"},{"en":"The seller is busy.","translation":"Penjualnya sedang sibuk.","hi":"The"},{"en":"An item is missing.","translation":"Ada satu barang yang kurang.","hi":"An"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"Mistake is here.","right":"The mistake is here."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"choice","kind":"choice","before":"","after":"mistake is here.","options":["A","An","The"],"answer":"The","why":"Kalian berdua tahu kesalahan yang mana: the."}}]},{"num":"12","title":"Tentang benda secara umum — tanpa a dan the","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Kalau bicara tentang jenis benda secara umum, bukan yang tertentu, cukup kata dengan s: Books are heavy — «buku itu berat» (buku apa pun). The magazines are new — majalah tertentu yang kalian berdua lihat."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"Books are heavy.","translation":"Buku itu berat. *(secara umum)*","hi":"Books"},{"en":"Newspapers are cheap.","translation":"Koran itu murah. *(secara umum)*","hi":"Newspapers"},{"en":"Wrenches are expensive.","translation":"Kunci pas itu mahal. *(secara umum)*","hi":"Wrenches"},{"en":"The magazines are new.","translation":"Majalahnya baru. *(yang ini)*","hi":"The"},{"en":"The stairs are narrow.","translation":"Tangganya sempit. *(di gedung ini)*","hi":"The"}]}]},{"num":"13","title":"Warna dan ciri — di DEPAN benda","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Kita bilang «cangkir merah» — warnanya di belakang. Bahasa Inggris kebalikannya: warna di depan — a red cup. Warna tidak pernah pakai s: black chairs. a atau an dipilih dari bunyi kata tepat sesudahnya: an olive coat."},{"kind":"formula","formula":[{"text":"a / an / this / these","accent":true},{"text":"warna atau ciri","accent":true},{"text":"benda","accent":true}]},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"It is a red cup.","translation":"Ini cangkir merah.","hi":"red"},{"en":"It is an olive coat.","translation":"Ini mantel hijau zaitun.","hi":"an"},{"en":"These are black chairs.","translation":"Ini kursi-kursi hitam.","hi":"black"},{"en":"This round table is heavy.","translation":"Meja bundar ini berat.","hi":"round"},{"en":"These metal boxes are heavy.","translation":"Kotak-kotak logam ini berat.","hi":"metal"},{"en":"This striped scarf is new.","translation":"Syal bergaris ini baru.","hi":"striped"}]},{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"It is a cup red.","right":"It is a red cup."},{"wrong":"These are blacks chairs.","right":"These are black chairs."},{"wrong":"It is a olive coat.","right":"It is an olive coat."}]},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"word_bank","kind":"word_bank","prompt":"Penjual bertanya cangkir mana yang kamu mau. Katakan: «Ini cangkir merah».","answer":["It","is","a","red","cup"],"slotLabels":["siapa","penjepit","satu","warna","apa"],"distractors":["an","reds"]}}]},{"num":"14","title":"Kesalahan yang dibuat hampir semua orang","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"fix","fixes":[{"wrong":"It is chair.","right":"It is a chair."},{"wrong":"They are ticket.","right":"They are tickets."},{"wrong":"It is a oven.","right":"It is an oven."},{"wrong":"Album this is big.","right":"This album is big."},{"wrong":"This are shoes.","right":"These are shoes."},{"wrong":"Mistake is here.","right":"The mistake is here."},{"wrong":"It is a cup red.","right":"It is a red cup."}]},{"kind":"tip","text":"Sebelum menyebut benda, tanya dirimu dua hal. Satu atau banyak? Satu — a/an, this/that. Banyak — s di akhir, these/those, are. Lalu: pendengar sudah tahu yang mana? Kalau ya — the."},{"kind":"drill","drill":{"type":"binary","kind":"binary","question":"Kemeja-kemeja ada di depanmu. Mana yang benar?","optionA":"This shirts are clean.","optionB":"These shirts are clean.","correct":"B","explain":"Kemejanya banyak dan dekat: these."}}]},{"num":"15","title":"Bekal untuk latihan","defaultOpen":false,"blocks":[{"kind":"body","text":"Satu benda — a atau an sesuai bunyi pertama. Banyak — s, tanpa a. Dekat — this / these, jauh — that / those, selalu di depan. Yang kalian berdua tahu — the. Warna dan ciri di depan benda: a red cup."},{"kind":"examples","examples":[{"en":"It is an hour.","translation":"Satu jam.","hi":"an"},{"en":"They are batteries.","translation":"Ini baterai.","hi":"batteries"},{"en":"Those flowers are fresh.","translation":"Bunga-bunga itu segar.","hi":"Those"},{"en":"The mistake is here.","translation":"Kesalahannya di sini.","hi":"The"},{"en":"It is a red cup.","translation":"Ini cangkir merah.","hi":"red"}]}]}],"sessionSection":{"1":"02","2":"02","3":"02","4":"02","5":"02","6":"02","7":"02","8":"02","9":"03","10":"03","11":"04","12":"04","13":"04","14":"04","15":"04","16":"04","17":"05","18":"05","19":"07","20":"07","21":"07","22":"07","23":"07","24":"07","25":"08","26":"08","27":"08","28":"08","29":"08","30":"08","31":"08","32":"08","33":"09","34":"09","35":"10","36":"10","37":"10","38":"10","39":"10","40":"10","41":"11","42":"11","43":"12","44":"12","45":"12","46":"12","47":"12","48":"12","49":"13","50":"13","51":"13","52":"13","53":"13","54":"13","55":"13","56":"13"}}
